:answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509235}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5d211815-c8ae-5268-9f21-aa7a3a361a49" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n$\\{s + 5t = 8; -6s - 3t = -11$\nDescribe the steps needed to eliminate the variable $s$ from the system:\n\nTo eliminate $s$, multiply the\n{{field-1}}\nequation by\n{{field-2}},\nand add the equations." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $s$ in the first equation is $1$, while in the second equation it is $-6$.\n\nIf we multiply the first equation by ${\\color{blue}6}$, then the coefficient of $s$ will turn into $6$, which will cancel with the coefficient of $-6$ in the second equation.\n\n$$\n\\{(s + 5t = 8)\\cdot (6); -6s - 3t = -11\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $s$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n6s + 30t &= 48 \\\\\n-6s - 3t &= -11 \\\\\n(30t - 3t) &= (48 - 11) \\\\\n27t &= 37\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is the following:\n\n> *To eliminate $s$, multiply the $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\text{first}}$ equation by $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}6}$, and add the equations*."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509176 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192654 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "93dcc73c-ce2d-5fa3-b32b-9fc600fb269e" :knowledge-point/title "Eliminating the First Variable" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050190 :topic/title "Solving Systems of Linear Equations Using Elimination: One Transformation"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1b6c98e2-b881-582d-9f5f-0b5e631af0d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "second" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509136} {:answer/id #uuid "41817a51-4551-5887-8edc-4f68222f6c52" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :a