equation by\n{{field-2}},\nand add the equations." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $u$ in the first equation is $-1$, while in the second equation it is $5$.\n\nIf we multiply the first equation by ${\\color{blue}5}$, then the coefficient of $u$ will turn into $-5$, which will cancel with the coefficient of $5$ in the second equation.\n\n$$\n\\{(-u + 7v = 0)\\cdot (5); 5u + 6v = -3\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $u$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-5u + 35v &= 0 \\\\\n5u + 6v &= -3 \\\\\n(35v + 6v) &= (0 - 3) \\\\\n41v &= -3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is the following:\n\n> *To eliminate $u$, multiply the $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\text{first}}$ equation by $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}5}$, and add the equations*."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509185 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192654 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "93dcc73c-ce2d-5fa3-b32b-9fc600fb269e" :knowledge-point/title "Eliminating the First Variable" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050190 :topic/title "Solving Systems of Linear Equations Using Elimination: One Transformation"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "38a5e8cf-9679-5e37-af4f-2b17615357b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509148} {:answer/id #uuid "5f107f49-ca98-5c5c-ba01-7ed409d9584c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509167} {:answer/id #uuid "cab95ace-4eda-5db9-84f4-6e8b591ffd8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509209} {:answer/id #uuid "f64438e6-d808-5371-8b19-8ad9d9da997a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509231}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cab95ace-4eda-5db9-84f4-6e8b591ffd8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509209} :answer-field/id #uuid "9a877f6f-f677-54d3-8e13-f1e41a168341" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509196} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5508c343-1cde-52e2-b519-45724995255d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "first" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509158} {:answer/id #uuid "634fb5d2-df05-5b0b-b07f-054996dc4e91" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "second" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509169}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5508c343-1cde-52e2-b519-45724995255d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "first" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509158} :answer-field/id #uuid "e8160bd8-72f0-543f-a4bb-48e47b164659" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509221}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7a39a169-0a8a-5634-a2bd-69230a2e80b3" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n$\\{-x + 6y = -10; 3x - 6y = -10$\nDescribe the steps needed to eliminate the variable $x$ from the system:\n\nTo eliminate $x$, multiply the\n{{field-1}}\nequation by\n{{field-2}},\nand add the equations." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $x$ in the first equation is $-1$, while in the second equation it is $3$.\n\nIf we multiply the first equation by ${\\color{blue}3}$, then the coefficient of $x$ will turn into $-3$, which will cancel with the coefficient of $3$ in the second equation.\n\n$$\n\\{(-x + 6y = -10)\\cdot (3); 3x - 6y = -10\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $x$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-3x + 18y &= -30 \\\\\n3x - 6y &= -10 \\\\\n(18y - 6y) &= (-30 - 10) \\\\\n12y &= -40\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is the following:\n\n> *To eliminate $x$, multiply the $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\text{first}}$ equation by $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}3}$, and add the equations*."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509190 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192654 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "93dcc73c-ce2d-5fa3-b32b-9fc600fb269e" :knowledge-point/title "Eliminating the First Variable" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050190 :topic/title "Solving Systems of Linear Equations Using Elimination: One Transformation"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c7580cd-b447-5b07-8244-aa60ed8b432b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "second" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509127} {:answer/id #uuid "37f6dc11-926d-5c03-9805-d02d2532713f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "first" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509146}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0c7580cd-b447-5b07-8244-aa60ed8b432b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "second" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509127} :answer-field/id #uuid "38297468-7ab5-5b91-8e12-ca8efeca13e3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509147} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1aec4d68-692c-572d-ac3c-b01bfca6be6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509135} {:answer/id #uuid "91e3d394-d205-5608-b462-7568316fcc28" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509193} {:answer/id #uuid "d4fbe5d2-a01c-5b88-b8b7-675b4ad0be31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509213} {:answer/id #uuid "f0d2b2ff-1278-5e85-9a71-91debd3eb472" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509227}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d4fbe5d2-a01c-5b88-b8b7-675b4ad0be31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509213} :answer-field/id #uuid "8f99a074-f636-5d4f-ba30-33d540aa5e50" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509191}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "8c460209-35ec-5be6-8f7c-2d8bae28aa03" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n$\\{15u - 6v = -10; 3u - 8v = -12$\nDescribe the steps needed to eliminate the variable $u$ from the system:\n\nTo eliminate $u$, multiply the\n{{field-1}}\nequation by\n{{field-2}},\nand add the equations." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $u$ in the first equation is $15$, while in the second equation it is $3$.\n\nIf we multiply the second equation by ${\\color{blue}-5}$, then the coefficient of $u$ will turn into $-15$, which will cancel with the coefficient of $15$ in the first equation.\n\n$$\n\\{15u - 6v = -10; (3u - 8v = -12)\\cdot (-5)\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $u$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n15u - 6v &= -10 \\\\\n-15u + 40v &= 60 \\\\\n(-6v + 40v) &= (-10 + 60) \\\\\n34v &= 50\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is the following:\n\n> *To eliminate $u$, multiply the $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\text{second}}$ equation by $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}-5}$, and add the equations*."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509195 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192654 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "93dcc73c-ce2d-5fa3-b32b-9fc600fb269e" :knowledge-point/title "Eliminating the First Variable" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050190 :topic/title "Solving Systems of Linear Equations Using Elimination: One Transformation"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f820aee-0719-5afc-b3d3-14f46271246a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "first" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509128} {:answer/id #uuid "cbac78f7-7dff-51a3-a55d-073dd5230aa9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "second" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509210}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0f820aee-0719-5afc-b3d3-14f46271246a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "first" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509128} :answer-field/id #uuid "81d462b8-3d66-5697-a0a9-ce9f3b971dc7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509186} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6334e086-8b3a-50b5-b74a-5e58a1f303d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509168} {:answer/id #uuid "6d29c62b-38b6-5ce1-be65-5e45063442ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509177} {:answer/id #uuid "d671f6e8-f7b3-56b5-bad6-17a0efd3bf06" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509214} {:answer/id #uuid "ec19c76d-a858-564f-9af1-2f6e9abf02bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509225}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6334e086-8b3a-50b5-b74a-5e58a1f303d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509168} :answer-field/id #uuid "f3a1b3a8-cba2-54ff-8adf-5a22cd277c15" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509229}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "97244e8f-197f-58ca-8655-e2235fc7d882" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n$\\{-2s + 10t = 5; -8s - 2t = 10$\nDescribe the steps needed to eliminate the variable $s$ from the system:\n\nTo eliminate $s$, multiply the\n{{field-1}}\nequation by\n{{field-2}},\nand add the equations." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $s$ in the first equation is $-2$, while in the second equation it is $-8$.\n\nIf we multiply the first equation by ${\\color{blue}-4}$, then the coefficient of $s$ will turn into $8$, which will cancel with the coefficient of $-8$ in the second equation.\n\n$$\n\\{(-2s + 10t = 5)\\cdot (-4); -8s - 2t = 10\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $s$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n8s - 40t &= -20 \\\\\n-8s - 2t &= 10 \\\\\n(-40t - 2t) &= (-20 + 10) \\\\\n-42t &= -10\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is the following:\n\n> *To eliminate $s$, multiply the $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\text{first}}$ equation by $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}-4}$, and add the equations*."}]}
